{"test_id":"distractor_941094","arm":"distractor_reject","source_timestamp":1775679948,"formatted_timestamp":"20:25, 04/08/2026","user_query":"static cling on my clothes is brutal in winter, fix?","prior_conversation":[],"action":"asked_chatbot","source_hashtags":[],"held_out_preference":null,"blind_check_score":null,"blind_check_generic_answer":null,"privacy_flagged_prefs":[{"persona_item":"Engages with hip-hop radio and media content, especially outlets like Hot 97.","category":"hip-hop media"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys 1990s golden-era hip-hop.","category":"hip-hop music"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys Disney-owned franchise shows and movies, especially Marvel and Star Wars titles.","category":"film and tv fandom"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys classic hip-hop culture and legacy rap figures.","category":"hip-hop culture"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys comedy and satirical entertainment.","category":"comedy entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys comedy content on social media.","category":"comedy entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys hip-hop dance content and dance challenge videos.","category":"dance"}],"top_k_relevant_prefs":[],"gt_slice":{"target":[],"avoid":[],"t_test":1775679948,"window_seconds":86400},"post_test_window":{"post_test_positives":[],"post_test_negatives":[]},"irrelevant_persona_items":["Engages with hip-hop radio and media content, especially outlets like Hot 97.","Enjoys 1990s golden-era hip-hop.","Enjoys Disney-owned franchise shows and movies, especially Marvel and Star Wars titles.","Enjoys classic hip-hop culture and legacy rap figures.","Enjoys comedy and satirical entertainment.","Enjoys comedy content on social media.","Enjoys hip-hop dance content and dance challenge videos."],"_distractor_reject":true,"example_response":"Static cling gets worse in dry winter air, so try using a little less dryer heat, add wool dryer balls or a damp washcloth for the last few minutes, and use a dryer sheet or anti-static spray. You can also moisturize fabrics by line-drying a bit or rubbing a metal hanger over clingy clothes before you put them on.","groundtruth_preference":"Preferences in profile that must NOT be surfaced (any of them):
  (none identified)

Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"Directly addresses the static cling problem with multiple practical fixes."},"inferior_response":{"text":"Winter static usually comes from dry air, so start by cutting dryer heat a bit and tossing in wool balls or a damp towel for the last 5–10 minutes. A quick mist of anti-static spray helps, and if you want a cleaner fix, line-drying partway can make clothes feel less clingy. It’s a bit like getting ready for dance: smoother fabrics just move better.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"dance"}}}

