Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"It directly answers the question with practical name-remembering tips."},"inferior_response":{"text":"I usually say the person’s name once right after we meet, then sneak it into the next sentence or two so it feels natural. If it helps, I’ll pair it with a mental hook, kind of like how boxing fandom sticks when a matchup is memorable.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"boxing fandom"}}}
